    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The ratio contains \\(2+4+6=12\\) equal shares. The smallest part is therefore \\[ 64\\left(\\frac{2}{12}\\right)=\\frac{32}{3}=10\\frac{2}{3}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Add the three numbers in the ratio to find the total number of equal shares",
        "The smallest part is \\(\\dfrac{2}{2+4+6}\\) of \\(64\\)"
      ],
